From ff775248d2683b5bc62a84866ba0832f6a47ede2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 12:41:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] About: show the public patch count on a local image; Warden:
 prefixes loaded moves to the count bar; dict keys for v2.6.7

About (field): every flashed image read a dash for "patches applied"
because the build stamped a count only when the public series' tip was
the build's own version - and the owner runs the local images, which are
always built BEFORE their cut. The build now always stamps the series
count plus the version the series is as of; the page prints the plain
count when they match and "N / series as of vX" when the image is ahead
of its cut. Never the previous cut's count passed off as this one's.
(Build side: build-scripts/_reaper_build_lib.sh + gen_provenance.sh in
the lean repo, synced to the engine.)

Warden (field): the "N prefixes loaded" figure is a size, not a health
signal; it moves from the Countries Blocked tile to the per-type count
bar next to Countries / Threat feeds / Unclassified. The amber "N empty"
warning stays on the tile.

Dicts: RVR_54/54b/55/56/57/58 (policy routing), RABT_42, RWDN_89 - English
in all 25 packs per the standing decision; lockstep 6717 lines.
